Keeps Rooster off every server Helium hosts.

Helium's services (extension proxy, !bangs, spellcheck dictionaries, browser
and component updates) run on imput's infrastructure and are switched on by
consent during Helium's onboarding. Rooster has no onboarding and runs no
services backend, so services are always off, and the hard-coded Helium
endpoints (services origin, update feed, crash server, extension ping domain)
point nowhere. The services code stays compiled because later Helium patches
build on it; a Rooster backend can replace these defaults later.

